//go:build ignore

// Historical reference only. This file is deliberately not valid runtime wiring.
// See ../README.md before using any part of it in a future redesign.
package commentemailnotifications

// HistoricalConfig records the fields that the retired SiteConfig model used.
// A future implementation must define a separate extension-owned configuration
// model instead of restoring these fields to the core site_configs table.
type HistoricalConfig struct {
	Enabled           bool
	AdminNotifyAll    bool
	ReplyFromName     string
	AdminSubjectPrefix string
	ReplySubjectPrefix string
	ReplyTextTemplate  string
	AdminTextTemplate  string
	SiteURL            string
	ReplyHTMLTemplate  string
	AdminHTMLTemplate  string
}

/*
Historical PostComment behavior, intentionally preserved as documentation:

  if SMTP and interaction email were enabled:
    - a top-level comment or guestbook entry notified smtpFrom, falling back
      to smtpUser;
    - a reply also notified that address when AdminNotifyAll was enabled;
    - a direct parent author was notified only when the account email was
      verified, the reply was not self-authored, and the author could still
      view the new reply;
    - {site}, {user}, {content}, and {url} were replaced with strings;
    - an HTML template, when present, replaced the text body entirely;
    - send errors were discarded and SMTP delivery ran inside the request.

This behavior is not safe or complete enough to restore. A future extension
must use escaped templates, an explicit management recipient, asynchronous
delivery with timeouts/retries, and durable delivery audit records.
*/
